# .shellcheckrc — shared shellcheck configuration for TestAtlas
#
# Plan 07-02 (INSTALL-02). Defaults are strict; selectively disabled codes
# below have rationales documented per-line. Document long-form in
# CONTRIBUTING.md (TODO Plan 07-05).
enable=all

# SC2244: Prefer explicit -n to check non-empty variable. We use [ -n "$X" ]
# explicitly where it matters; this disable is reserved for cases that read
# more naturally as bare-string tests (none yet, kept for forward-compat).
# SC1090: Can't follow non-constant source. We don't `source` anything inside
# install.sh, but adapter authors may extend later — disabled defensively.
# SC2250 (style): Prefer ${var} braces even when not required. POSIX `$var`
# inside double-quotes is unambiguous; the unbraced form is the dominant
# nvm/install.sh style. Bare-style preference, not correctness.
# SC2310 (info): Function invoked under `!` disables `set -e`. We use `if !
# _download` deliberately for the npm→GitHub-Releases fallback; the inner
# return code is handled explicitly.
# SC2312 (info): Consider invoking command separately to avoid masking return
# value. Inline `$(node -v)` in error logs is human-readable; the failure
# path doesn't depend on its return code.
# SC2249 (info): Consider adding a default *) case. Our --global flag detect
# is a single-pattern match; absence of a default branch is the contract.
disable=SC2244,SC1090,SC2250,SC2310,SC2312,SC2249
